Prior to this, the distorted surface was usually obtained by Bessel fitting, and pre-distortion information was obtained by the inverse solution process. Surface fitting introduces unnecessary errors, resulting in a reduction in prediction accuracy. Particularly, the improvement in fitting accuracy leads to an exponential increase in calculation memory, so a more accurate result will sacrifice larger storage demand. We can, however, output pre-distortion information directly from neural network prediction, and eliminate the step of surface fitting, by decoupling disparity and distortion.
